# Patches in `patches/` are matched byte-for-byte against a freshly cloned
# Google Benchmark tree, so their line endings must not depend on the platform
# that checked them out. Without this, a Windows checkout with
# `core.autocrlf=true` rewrites them to CRLF while the fetched upstream tree
# stays LF (or vice versa), and every hunk fails with "patch does not apply".
# See the matching `GIT_CONFIG` on the FetchContent_Declare in CMakeLists.txt,
# which pins the other side of the comparison to LF.
*.patch -text
